WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:11.928
-[bells chime]
-[chalk scrapes]

00:12.012 --> 00:13.722
EDUCATIONAL RIGHTS PROTECTION BUREAU

00:13.805 --> 00:15.807
ALL REPORTS
ARE KEPT CONFIDENTIAL AS A RULE

00:15.890 --> 00:18.685
PLEASE HELP OUR SCHOOL
THIS JUST ISN'T RIGHT

00:18.768 --> 00:20.395
THIS IS DAILY LIFE AT OUR SCHOOL

00:20.478 --> 00:21.730
IT'S REALLY MESSED UP

00:21.813 --> 00:22.939
PLEASE COME HELP, ERPB

00:23.023 --> 00:25.025
[uneasy music plays]

00:26.151 --> 00:28.653
I FEEL SO BAD FOR OUR TEACHER

00:34.993 --> 00:36.953
EXPOSING THE STUDENT
WHO ASSAULTED A TEACHER

00:37.454 --> 00:39.330
REPORTING A SERIOUS ASSAULT ON A TEACHER

00:39.414 --> 00:40.707
[gasps]

00:48.548 --> 00:52.427
We have recently discovered that
the reason behind the creation of the ERPB

00:52.510 --> 00:55.221
was the death of a young teacher
around two years ago.

00:55.305 --> 00:56.598
This teacher, as we have learned,

00:56.681 --> 00:59.309
was the daughter
of the current Minister of Education

00:59.392 --> 01:02.187
and founder of ERPB, Choi Gang-Seok.

01:02.270 --> 01:05.774
It has also come to light that the teacher
was the fiancée of inspector Na Hwa-jin.

01:07.984 --> 01:11.112
Are we to believe that
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau

01:11.196 --> 01:13.782
was born of moral conviction
and noble ideals?

01:13.865 --> 01:17.494
These individuals are not guided
by good faith or public service.

01:17.577 --> 01:21.873
Their actions are motivated solely
by revenge and a thirst for retribution.

01:22.373 --> 01:23.958
This is a personal vendetta.

01:28.963 --> 01:30.048
[Hwa-jin] Im Han-rim.

01:31.091 --> 01:32.509
[music fades]

01:32.592 --> 01:33.593
What are you doing?

01:33.676 --> 01:36.679
-I was just watching something.
-Oh, okay.

01:37.847 --> 01:38.765
Let's go.

01:38.848 --> 01:40.767
Sir, did you see what happened

01:41.267 --> 01:42.894
at the press conference?

01:48.274 --> 01:49.400
Yeah.

01:53.279 --> 01:54.948
Is it true what they said?

01:55.740 --> 01:56.991
Yes, it's all true.

02:04.332 --> 02:08.294
Han-rim, if we keep standing here,
we'll be late for our meeting. Come on.

02:11.047 --> 02:13.091
[keyboard clacks]

02:13.174 --> 02:15.635
[Geun-dae] None of them are here
when we have all this work.

02:17.178 --> 02:18.304
[sighs]

02:19.806 --> 02:20.849
[sighs]

02:20.932 --> 02:23.893
This team doesn't offer any

02:23.977 --> 02:26.855
room for growth or learning due to

02:26.938 --> 02:30.275
its ignorant and unprofessional nature.

02:30.775 --> 02:32.902
Add to this, the tyrannical leadership,

02:32.986 --> 02:37.657
and I truly can't foresee
any room for growth in my current role.

02:37.740 --> 02:40.118
"I am therefore requesting
a transfer of assignment."

02:40.201 --> 02:43.663
[sputters] I was just…

02:43.746 --> 02:44.789
[funky music plays]

02:44.873 --> 02:46.916
[sighs]

02:48.001 --> 02:49.419
Deputy Director Geun-dae.

02:50.170 --> 02:51.212
Yes?

02:51.296 --> 02:53.089
What is this font you're using?

02:53.590 --> 02:55.175
You can read it all so clearly.

02:56.384 --> 02:57.218
Sir?

02:57.302 --> 03:00.388
Let's start using this font
on all official documents from now on.

03:01.389 --> 03:02.932
[Geun-dae exhales]

03:04.350 --> 03:05.476
[sighs]

03:05.560 --> 03:06.603
-[Gang-seok] Oh…
-[gasps]

03:07.103 --> 03:10.023
And, Deputy… [chuckles]

03:10.106 --> 03:11.858
…the request you put in won't work.

03:12.483 --> 03:14.360
If you want to transfer
out of this department,

03:14.444 --> 03:15.904
find something better to convince me.

03:15.987 --> 03:19.115
You'll have to come up
with some real reasons to leave.

03:19.616 --> 03:23.077
So anything less than that
just sounds like whining to me, you know?

03:25.663 --> 03:26.581
Good morning, sir.

03:26.664 --> 03:28.958
Both of you need to get a move on!
We don't have all day!

03:29.042 --> 03:31.961
-Look at the time!
-[gasps]

03:35.548 --> 03:36.507
Safe.

03:43.765 --> 03:45.558
[exhales slowly]

03:45.642 --> 03:47.393
[Geun-dae] We just received a report.

03:47.477 --> 03:50.563
It's from Chukmyeong
Foreign Language School,

03:51.064 --> 03:54.108
where one of the students
assaulted their teacher.

03:54.192 --> 03:57.362
Pretty seriously, as you can see.
There he is on the screen now.

03:57.445 --> 03:59.989
Our informant for this report
is a fellow educator

04:00.073 --> 04:02.367
who was there when the assault happened.

04:02.450 --> 04:05.328
They were also able to send
video proof of the incident.

04:05.411 --> 04:07.330
-Play the video, please.
-Yes, sir.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.877
[teacher] Park Hyeon-ung!
What do you think you're doing?

04:12.961 --> 04:15.171
You're a good student.
Doesn't mean you can act like this.

04:15.255 --> 04:17.257
[teacher groans]

04:17.340 --> 04:19.425
[students clamor]

04:19.509 --> 04:22.345
Mr. Cheon, are you okay?
What's the matter with you?

04:22.428 --> 04:23.346
[tense music plays]

04:23.429 --> 04:25.473
-[boy 1] What happened?
-Hyeon-ung, why?

04:25.556 --> 04:26.891
-[groans]
-[man] That's enough.

04:26.975 --> 04:28.685
[boy 2] Mr. Cheon, are you okay?

04:32.438 --> 04:34.440
TEACH YOU A LESSON

04:34.524 --> 04:37.986
CHUKMYEONG FOREIGN LANGUAGE HIGH SCHOOL

04:38.069 --> 04:40.321
Whoa. This is a high school?

04:41.072 --> 04:43.408
I don't think
I've ever seen one like this before.

04:43.491 --> 04:45.034
Mm-hmm. I know, right.

04:45.118 --> 04:48.246
[Han-rim] I heard they were the best,
even among international high schools,

04:48.329 --> 04:49.914
but this is impressive.

04:50.415 --> 04:53.501
How about you guys go ahead.
I'll catch up with you in a minute.

04:54.961 --> 04:56.004
You heard him.

04:57.338 --> 05:00.008
Getting into university
doesn't only depend on your grades.

05:00.091 --> 05:01.301
Like Seoul National University.

05:01.384 --> 05:04.178
[Mr. Cheon] I took a look
at this particular student's report

05:04.262 --> 05:05.471
and saw that his public…

05:05.555 --> 05:07.807
Did you know that this school
actually only recently

05:07.890 --> 05:11.519
came to be known as one of the top
international high schools in the country?

05:11.602 --> 05:13.104
This rapid rise was mainly due

05:13.187 --> 05:15.732
to the arrival of their star teacher,
Mr. Cheon Sang-yeol.

05:15.815 --> 05:19.485
With his classes, students started to be
accepted into prestigious universities,

05:19.569 --> 05:21.571
which turned this school
into what it is today.

05:21.654 --> 05:23.197
This was all due to his hard work.

05:23.281 --> 05:25.408
So, he's good
at getting students into uni?

05:25.491 --> 05:30.997
It's more about his passion for teaching,
and his attitude, and being a role model.

05:31.080 --> 05:32.540
Role model?

05:32.623 --> 05:34.250
[Mr. Cheon] …as a teacher is difficult…

05:34.334 --> 05:35.877
So, why would someone hit him?

05:35.960 --> 05:38.046
[man] Not at all.
What you're accomplishing…

05:38.129 --> 05:41.883
[Hwa-jin] I'm sorry to bother you, sir,
but I've always wanted to meet you.

05:41.966 --> 05:45.678
I promised myself years ago that if I ever
got the chance to meet you, I'd thank you.

05:45.762 --> 05:46.888
-Oh, is that so?
-Yeah.

05:46.971 --> 05:47.930
-[laughs]
-Oh.

05:48.514 --> 05:50.058
[Hwa-jin] Allow me to introduce myself.

05:50.141 --> 05:54.145
I'm an inspector with the ERPB.
My name is Na Hwa-jin.

05:54.228 --> 05:55.188
Good afternoon.

05:55.271 --> 05:57.357
[Hwa-jin] It's actually thanks
to your online lectures

05:57.440 --> 06:00.276
that I was accepted
into the Military Academy.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.571
Well, I won't take all the credit.
I'm sure you worked very hard for it.

06:03.654 --> 06:07.825
Actually, sir, um, I'm sorry to ask this,
but you repeated this one phrase…

06:08.409 --> 06:09.327
Um…

06:09.827 --> 06:11.662
Wow, I can't believe this. [laughs]

06:11.746 --> 06:14.874
-[Mr. Cheon] Is everything all right?
-What the hell?

06:14.957 --> 06:17.502
Why is he fanboying over him like this?

06:18.086 --> 06:21.255
[clamoring on video]

06:32.183 --> 06:35.353
Inspector, can we act
like this never happened?

06:35.436 --> 06:37.730
The midterm exams
are just around the corner.

06:37.814 --> 06:40.316
You're aware of how critical they are
for Hyeon-ung and others.

06:40.400 --> 06:43.945
I understand, but Hyeon-ung's actions
cannot go unpunished, sir.

06:44.737 --> 06:46.072
[inhales]

06:46.155 --> 06:47.490
[sighs]

06:49.742 --> 06:51.119
Can I ask you one thing?

06:52.036 --> 06:54.622
Sorry if I'm overstepping,
but I really have to ask.

06:55.665 --> 06:57.125
Sure. Go ahead.

06:57.208 --> 06:59.210
If you don't mind,
could you please tell me

06:59.293 --> 07:01.879
that line that you were always repeating
at the end of your classes,

07:01.963 --> 07:03.756
when you'd say,
"Believe in your potential."

07:05.007 --> 07:06.592
-Seriously? [laughs]
-[Hwa-jin laughs]

07:06.676 --> 07:09.095
Well, I just couldn't
turn down the opportunity.

07:09.178 --> 07:11.764
-Especially when we have chalk right here.
-[laughs]

07:11.848 --> 07:14.142
So if you could just one more time?

07:14.225 --> 07:17.311
-Oh, I don't know, Inspector. [chuckles]
-[Hwa-jin laughs]

07:17.395 --> 07:18.479
-[Mr. Cheon grunts]
-Oh, damn

07:20.648 --> 07:22.650
You must believe in your potential.

07:23.359 --> 07:27.113
-[laughs]
-[chuckles]

07:27.196 --> 07:29.365
[Han-rim hums]

07:31.284 --> 07:32.702
[intriguing music plays]

07:35.371 --> 07:37.498
[laughs]

07:38.082 --> 07:39.333
[sighs]

07:42.211 --> 07:43.421
Whoa.

07:44.046 --> 07:47.091
-Oh, could you please not touch it?
-What is all of this?

07:47.175 --> 07:49.635
I bought it with what was left
of my first paycheck.

07:49.719 --> 07:52.555
A new… dual monitor setup.

07:52.638 --> 07:55.975
One of them is even a touch screen, and
can be mounted onto anything, anywhere.

07:56.058 --> 07:57.059
Isn't it awesome?

07:57.560 --> 07:58.978
Oh, it's just a computer.

07:59.896 --> 08:03.566
Well, it's actually much more than that.
It's a totally portable setup.

08:03.649 --> 08:06.277
The screen resolution is 16:9
and HD quality.

08:06.360 --> 08:09.405
Its 15.6-inch monitor makes it ideal
for watching any Netflix show you want.

08:09.489 --> 08:13.284
Also, the aspect ratio is optimized
for the perfect gaming experience.

08:14.243 --> 08:17.747
And you see this small thing over here?
It's a very unique USB-C port.

08:17.830 --> 08:20.500
This one outlet powers both
the power supply and the display output

08:20.583 --> 08:21.959
at the same time.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.337
So it's an expensive computer.

08:27.965 --> 08:30.301
Very nice. Super cool.

08:31.719 --> 08:32.720
[sighs]

08:32.803 --> 08:36.599
PATIENCE

08:36.682 --> 08:37.642
[music stops]

08:43.439 --> 08:44.440
[door closes]

08:50.821 --> 08:52.365
[Han-rim] So, you're Park Hyeon-ung?

08:52.865 --> 08:55.034
[clamoring on video]

08:56.160 --> 08:59.539
This is a video of you
assaulting your teacher, Mr. Cheon.

08:59.622 --> 09:00.790
Why did you do it?

09:02.375 --> 09:03.334
[breathes shakily]

09:03.417 --> 09:05.545
Even if I tell you why,
will you let me go?

09:06.796 --> 09:08.047
Of course you won't.

09:08.881 --> 09:11.926
If you're going to expel me, do it.
If you're going to report me, do it.

09:12.009 --> 09:13.803
Stop pretending you care.

09:19.433 --> 09:20.893
I see that you're hesitating.

09:21.394 --> 09:23.771
Would you like me
to make it easier for you?

09:30.278 --> 09:33.155
You would do well not to test my patience.

09:35.992 --> 09:37.743
The school hasn't decided yet

09:37.827 --> 09:40.663
on what measures to take
regarding Park Hyeon-ung's case.

09:40.746 --> 09:42.873
I was the one
who reported it to the Bureau,

09:42.957 --> 09:45.835
since I thought
you'd be able to find the right response.

09:45.918 --> 09:48.212
Everyone in this school admires Mr. Cheon.

09:48.296 --> 09:50.756
As a teacher,
there really isn't anybody quite like him.

09:51.882 --> 09:55.553
He's the kind of person who motivates you
to become the best teacher you can be.

09:56.846 --> 09:59.473
The reason our school
has gained the reputation that it has

09:59.557 --> 10:01.767
isn't just because he teaches well.

10:01.851 --> 10:04.020
He's the sort of teacher
who stays up all night with you

10:04.103 --> 10:06.731
as you wait for your letter of acceptance
from your dream university,

10:06.814 --> 10:08.941
and will be even happier than you
when you get accepted.

10:09.025 --> 10:12.028
That's why students
would die to have him as their teacher.

10:12.111 --> 10:14.905
And the fact that Hyeon-ung
would hit such a person,

10:14.989 --> 10:17.950
I just couldn't stand by and do nothing.

10:19.702 --> 10:20.703
Yeah.

10:22.872 --> 10:24.081
Oh!

10:25.291 --> 10:26.125
What's up?

10:29.670 --> 10:31.130
-Whoa.
-[Han-rim grunts]

10:31.213 --> 10:32.465
[punches thud]

10:32.548 --> 10:36.427
This damn kid! [breathes heavily]

10:39.221 --> 10:41.140
At what age do boys usually hit puberty?

10:41.223 --> 10:43.893
Puberty usually begins for boys
in their first year of middle school

10:43.976 --> 10:46.270
and ends around their second year
in high school.

10:46.354 --> 10:49.815
So, he's about to reach puberty. This kid
is so arrogant he won't even listen to me.

10:49.899 --> 10:53.903
How can he still be in school? He most
likely has terrible grades. What a bum.

10:53.986 --> 10:56.155
He's no bum.
You're jumping to conclusions.

10:56.238 --> 10:59.200
What I'm trying to say is
you might be judging him harshly.

10:59.784 --> 11:00.701
What do you mean?

11:01.869 --> 11:02.787
Park Hyeon-ung.

11:04.789 --> 11:05.873
He's the number one student.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.752
STUDENT REPORT CARD
NAME - PARK HYEON-UNG

11:09.835 --> 11:11.337
Are you kidding me?

11:11.420 --> 11:12.922
Now I'm even more confused.

11:13.923 --> 11:17.051
Why would he hit him? Why Mr. Cheon?

11:17.134 --> 11:19.136
[tense music plays]

11:25.226 --> 11:27.061
EXAM MANAGEMENT OFFICE

11:27.144 --> 11:28.187
[music fades]

11:29.480 --> 11:31.482
ENGLISH DEPARTMENT, TERM 1, 2026
MIDTERM EXAM

11:40.408 --> 11:42.493
VIEWING IS PROHIBITED
TO UNAUTHORIZED PERSONNEL

11:42.576 --> 11:43.494
Oh.

11:46.163 --> 11:47.415
Are these the upcoming exams?

11:49.208 --> 11:51.877
Yes, well, I keep an eye on them.

11:51.961 --> 11:54.338
It's part of my job
as Head of Academic Affairs.

11:54.422 --> 11:58.426
[laughs] Wow, so the exam papers
are all here.

11:58.509 --> 12:01.178
It's funny how, back in the day,
instead of studying for my exams,

12:01.262 --> 12:03.597
I'd dream about stealing them
with my friends.

12:03.681 --> 12:04.640
[both laugh]

12:04.724 --> 12:06.642
It was more fun
to come up with ways to steal them

12:06.726 --> 12:08.978
than to actually study for them. [laughs]

12:09.061 --> 12:10.938
I had those same dreams. Mm.

12:11.021 --> 12:12.523
You don't say so?

12:12.606 --> 12:14.567
Whoa, Mr. Cheon. That can't be true?

12:14.650 --> 12:17.027
Well, we can't stay here.
Why don't we head out?

12:17.111 --> 12:20.030
You're telling me you and I grew up
with the same dreams?

12:20.114 --> 12:21.198
[both laugh]

12:21.991 --> 12:25.870
[Hwa-jin] Mr. Cheon, do you have any idea
why Park Hyeon-ung might've attacked you?

12:27.413 --> 12:29.415
[sighs] I don't know.

12:29.498 --> 12:31.125
Is there anything that comes to mind?

12:34.128 --> 12:37.506
I recently created
a special class for gifted kids.

12:37.590 --> 12:39.425
Was Hyeon-Ung part of that classroom?

12:40.134 --> 12:41.552
[Mr. Cheon] He used to join us.

12:41.635 --> 12:44.513
But, as time went on, it was clear
that the curriculum we were studying

12:44.597 --> 12:45.806
was not up to his level.

12:46.307 --> 12:49.226
Like we saw a few minutes ago,
we need to solve this part first.

12:49.310 --> 12:50.895
Sir, we've already been over this.

12:50.978 --> 12:53.564
These are the type of problems
we were solving in our first year.

12:53.647 --> 12:55.691
As we can see on the board, the chord AC--

12:55.775 --> 12:59.278
Sir, why do we only review the basics?
Will revising this even help us?

12:59.361 --> 13:01.739
We've been going over
the same things for days.

13:01.822 --> 13:03.157
Hyeon-ung, stay with us.

13:03.240 --> 13:04.158
[Mr. Cheon sighs]

13:04.241 --> 13:06.160
[somber music plays]

13:06.827 --> 13:09.330
The class wasn't created
with only him in mind.

13:09.830 --> 13:12.666
There were others
that wanted to study, you know?

13:12.750 --> 13:17.004
All the same, the class was created
for his benefit, too, right? [chuckles]

13:17.713 --> 13:18.839
I'm not sure.

13:19.757 --> 13:21.717
Who really knows in the end? [chuckles]

13:22.218 --> 13:23.928
DETAILED SCHOOL LIFE RECORD

13:24.595 --> 13:26.180
[sighs] What do you wanna know?

13:26.263 --> 13:29.308
You need to help me understand
why you would do such a thing.

13:29.391 --> 13:30.226
[music fades]

13:30.309 --> 13:32.853
Why would the top student
assault his teacher?

13:36.148 --> 13:38.192
Hyeon-ung, it simply
doesn't make any sense

13:38.275 --> 13:41.987
that a smart kid like you wouldn't
understand the weight of his actions.

13:42.071 --> 13:44.824
I want to know what in God's name
pushed you to hit him?

13:48.410 --> 13:51.872
With your grades, you could easily
go to any top university with a full ride.

13:51.956 --> 13:55.209
You've studied from elementary
to high school, became the top student,

13:55.292 --> 13:57.002
just to throw it all away?

13:57.086 --> 14:00.256
You poured your blood, sweat and tears
into this, and now you have nothing.

14:01.382 --> 14:04.844
Have you even thought about your parents
and the sacrifices they made?

14:10.975 --> 14:12.101
[cries]

14:15.104 --> 14:18.023
[Mr. Cheon] To be honest,
I made a mistake recently.

14:18.107 --> 14:19.608
[cries]

14:19.692 --> 14:23.070
Every year, I ask parents to come to
discuss universities for their children.

14:23.153 --> 14:25.948
But Hyeon-ung's parents live
in the country and weren't able to come,

14:26.031 --> 14:27.241
so I went myself.

14:27.324 --> 14:29.159
HYEON-UNG'S KOREAN BUFFET

14:30.369 --> 14:31.745
They were running their restaurant,

14:31.829 --> 14:34.290
and they were so busy
that I ended up just eating there

14:34.373 --> 14:36.375
since I didn't want to take up their time.

14:36.458 --> 14:37.293
How's that?

14:37.376 --> 14:38.627
[poignant music plays]

14:38.711 --> 14:39.628
[Han-rim] What?

14:40.129 --> 14:41.589
You haven't told them yet?

14:41.672 --> 14:43.924
[breathes shakily]

14:44.008 --> 14:46.719
I guess I'll be the one
to break the bad news to them.

14:47.428 --> 14:50.639
Don't you dare! You!

14:50.723 --> 14:52.016
[Hyeon-ung groans]

14:52.099 --> 14:54.393
[Hyeon-ung gasps] Let go!

14:54.476 --> 14:56.353
I said let go!

14:57.021 --> 14:58.689
[whimpers]

14:59.315 --> 15:00.566
Is this unfair?

15:01.358 --> 15:02.443
Feel powerless?

15:02.526 --> 15:04.528
Let me go now! [cries]

15:04.612 --> 15:05.529
Why?

15:05.613 --> 15:07.531
Then ask somebody for help.

15:08.699 --> 15:11.785
The first step to getting help
is asking for help.

15:11.869 --> 15:13.871
[cries]

15:17.249 --> 15:21.128
Excuse me, Hyeon-ung.
Your tuition still has not been paid yet.

15:22.880 --> 15:26.884
[man] Hey, champ! Your tuition for
this month hasn't been paid yet, has it?

15:26.967 --> 15:29.678
We've been so busy at the restaurant
that it slipped my mind.

15:29.762 --> 15:33.891
I'll take care of it soon, don't worry.
Focus on your studies. We believe in you!

15:33.974 --> 15:34.808
[sighs]

15:34.892 --> 15:37.019
[Hyeon-ung] After Mr. Cheon
visited our restaurant,

15:37.102 --> 15:39.021
we were suddenly ordered to close down.

15:39.104 --> 15:42.066
Apparently someone had complained
that we didn't have a license.

15:42.149 --> 15:44.151
[somber music plays]

15:46.695 --> 15:48.906
Is that why you assaulted Mr. Cheon?

15:54.203 --> 15:56.330
Even after the restaurant closed,

15:57.998 --> 16:01.669
my parents weren't ready to give up,
so they found me a private tutor.

16:01.752 --> 16:04.630
[Mr. Cheon] Wow, look at that.
You did great on this test.

16:04.713 --> 16:08.300
And this wasn't an easy exam.
You have a tutor?

16:09.301 --> 16:10.177
Yes, sir.

16:10.260 --> 16:13.389
That tutor of yours must be good.
What's their name?

16:14.181 --> 16:16.642
What? You're gonna stop tutoring me?

16:16.725 --> 16:19.728
I'm busy with my studies.
I need time for myself.

16:21.480 --> 16:25.526
So, right after Mr. Cheon got his name,
my tutor just suddenly decided to stop.

16:26.026 --> 16:27.444
You don't find that odd?

16:32.992 --> 16:34.159
[music fades]

16:36.203 --> 16:38.497
[Hwa-jin] Sir, may I ask
why you pick up these rocks?

16:38.580 --> 16:43.669
Well, our students are usually reading or
watching lectures when they're on campus.

16:44.169 --> 16:45.879
I won't be the one to tell them to stop,

16:45.963 --> 16:48.924
so I pick them up
to avoid them tripping and getting hurt.

16:49.883 --> 16:50.759
[exhales]

16:50.843 --> 16:52.177
[Hwa-jin] Ah.

16:53.095 --> 16:55.389
Well, now I know
why people keep calling for you

16:55.472 --> 16:57.558
to be Seoul's next
Superintendent of Education.

16:57.641 --> 17:00.352
Oh, don't say ridiculous things
like that, please, Inspector.

17:00.436 --> 17:02.021
By the way, sir, which, um…

17:02.688 --> 17:05.357
Which position is higher,
the Superintendent,

17:05.441 --> 17:06.900
or the Minister of Education?

17:07.985 --> 17:08.986
What?

17:09.069 --> 17:11.530
The Minister is doing all that he can,
to be fair.

17:12.406 --> 17:14.616
It's just that I think
some things could improve.

17:15.868 --> 17:18.370
I was just thinking, maybe in the future
I'll be working for you.

17:18.454 --> 17:20.039
[laughs]

17:20.122 --> 17:21.790
-I'm serious, Mr. Cheon.
-Stop it.

17:21.874 --> 17:23.667
[both laugh]

17:23.751 --> 17:26.545
By the way, uh, I was just wondering,

17:27.588 --> 17:29.006
what are you gonna do to Hyeon-ung?

17:30.966 --> 17:32.760
We will follow the usual protocol.

17:33.469 --> 17:34.428
[clicks tongue]

17:35.429 --> 17:37.306
I can't help but feel bad for him.

17:37.806 --> 17:40.642
But I guess punishment
might be the only way he'll learn.

17:42.603 --> 17:43.896
I'm sure you know best.

17:43.979 --> 17:47.274
The Bureau always knows best,
future Superintendent.

17:47.357 --> 17:49.818
Inspector, please, enough of that.
I'm just doing my job.

17:49.902 --> 17:52.112
-[Hwa-jin] It's the truth.
-[Mr. Cheon] You make me blush.

17:52.196 --> 17:54.907
Mr. Superintendent, I'll follow
your example by picking up rocks.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.241
Please, let me do it.

17:56.325 --> 17:59.203
-[Mr. Cheon] This is too much.
-[Hwa-jin] No, no this is my pleasure.

17:59.286 --> 18:02.748
[Mr. Cheon on video] Well, Min-woo, you're
quite popular with kids on the internet.

18:02.831 --> 18:04.958
Many of my students said I should come on.

18:05.042 --> 18:06.085
Ah, I see.

18:06.168 --> 18:07.920
-[Mr. Cheon] Hello, everyone.
-[laughs]

18:08.003 --> 18:09.630
[Mr. Cheon laughs]

18:09.713 --> 18:12.925
[Min-woo] …reputation as the best teacher
in South Korea. The effort you…

18:13.008 --> 18:14.843
Inspector, I interrogated Hyeon-ung,

18:14.927 --> 18:17.471
and I believe that it's important
for you to hear out his story.

18:17.554 --> 18:18.889
Boom-boom-bah!

18:19.515 --> 18:21.225
-Yeah!
-[Hwa-jin] The chalk snap.

18:21.308 --> 18:24.770
Hey, Han-rim, you know,
he actually did this for me earlier.

18:24.853 --> 18:26.063
Man, back in my day,

18:26.146 --> 18:29.149
everyone did his signature chalk snap
and final line for fun.

18:29.233 --> 18:31.527
[laughs]

18:32.861 --> 18:34.988
Why aren't you focusing on the assignment?

18:35.614 --> 18:38.033
You don't seem to be your usual self, sir.

18:38.117 --> 18:41.370
You don't seem to be interested
in solving this case.

18:41.453 --> 18:44.123
It seems Mr. Cheon is more important
than the mission of the Bureau.

18:44.206 --> 18:47.126
Or maybe the Bureau's mission
was different all along!

18:47.209 --> 18:50.212
[Min-woo] Something even more impressive
is that exams have gotten harder--

18:51.004 --> 18:52.256
What do you want me to say?

18:53.966 --> 18:54.842
[sighs]

18:58.929 --> 19:00.806
It seems you've already judged him.

19:02.599 --> 19:06.186
I have the impression that you believe
that the student is to blame.

19:06.270 --> 19:10.357
What I'm trying to say is, did you come
here having already made up your mind?

19:10.440 --> 19:12.568
Is what people are saying true?

19:15.279 --> 19:17.948
Your work with the Bureau,
is it only a personal vendetta?

19:25.789 --> 19:27.666
[Hwa-jin] If that's
what you're worried about,

19:28.333 --> 19:30.460
I'd like you to get back to work.

19:35.674 --> 19:36.842
[sighs]

19:38.302 --> 19:39.469
Im Han-rim,

19:40.762 --> 19:42.139
let's both stay focused, yeah?

19:58.447 --> 19:59.615
Shit!

20:05.245 --> 20:06.538
YEAR 3 STUDENT RANKINGS

20:09.124 --> 20:10.918
2ND - CHOI JI-HUN
TEACHER - MR. CHEON

20:12.252 --> 20:14.004
11TH - JUNG SU-JEONG
TEACHER - MR. CHEON

20:14.087 --> 20:15.631
[suspenseful music plays]

20:17.883 --> 20:20.469
NOAVIS INSTITUTE

20:22.429 --> 20:24.848
NOAVIS INSTITUTE

21:03.178 --> 21:04.304
-[music stops]
-[yelps]

21:04.388 --> 21:05.305
[man] Who are you?

21:05.389 --> 21:07.599
-[Geun-dae gasps]
-Who let you in here?

21:07.683 --> 21:11.353
Oh, I was just trying to find somebody
who could help me register.

21:11.436 --> 21:12.521
What school do you go to?

21:13.188 --> 21:17.150
-Chukmyeong Foreign Language School.
-Ah, so you go to Chukmyeong.

21:17.859 --> 21:18.860
-Yeah.
-[man exhales]

21:19.736 --> 21:21.822
Have you heard
anything interesting about our program?

21:22.781 --> 21:25.117
Sure. I heard
you were the best in the country.

21:25.742 --> 21:26.660
[chuckles softly]

21:27.327 --> 21:30.998
Unfortunately, our registration period
is over, and we're already fully booked.

21:31.081 --> 21:32.749
Oh, but how come?

21:32.833 --> 21:37.504
When I was looking, it seemed like
the classes were all empty, so I--

21:37.587 --> 21:39.298
You heard what I said, didn't you?

21:41.091 --> 21:44.344
Right, fully booked.
Sorry for the inconvenience.

21:53.061 --> 21:54.730
-[man] Wait a minute. Excuse me!
-Yeah?

21:55.772 --> 21:57.232
You told me you went to Chukmyeong?

21:57.316 --> 21:59.443
-Uh-huh.
-In what class?

21:59.526 --> 22:01.945
I'm in Class 4, specializing in English.

22:02.029 --> 22:04.573
Oh, then you must know
the class president, Moon Hyeon-o.

22:05.157 --> 22:07.951
Yes. Hyeon-o. Moon Hyeon-o.
I know him very well.

22:08.702 --> 22:10.912
Ah, my mistake. [chuckles]

22:11.496 --> 22:14.207
The class president for Class 4
is actually Bo-hyeon.

22:16.001 --> 22:20.130
Ah, you're right, it's Bo-hyeon.
Of course. I get them confused a lot.

22:20.213 --> 22:22.674
-How did you find out about us?
-Huh?

22:22.758 --> 22:25.552
-Are you even a student?
-Uh, wha… Of course.

22:25.635 --> 22:26.720
-Oh yeah?
-[Geun-dae] Y… Yes.

22:26.803 --> 22:28.347
-Who sent you?
-[Hyeong-ju] Geun-dae!

22:29.473 --> 22:32.225
-No way, Geun-dae!
-[Geun-dae] Whoa! Is that you Hyeong-ju?

22:32.809 --> 22:35.270
I'm pissed with you.
You didn't tell me when you transferred.

22:35.354 --> 22:39.524
-What school are you at now?
-I'm at Chukmyeong International School.

22:39.608 --> 22:41.943
-Did you cut your hair?
-[Hyeong-ju laughs]

22:42.027 --> 22:43.070
[Geun-dae] How've you been?

22:43.153 --> 22:44.363
I'm happy for you.

22:44.863 --> 22:47.741
I always knew it. You were made
for the top-performing high schools.

22:48.408 --> 22:49.701
How are things for you?

22:49.785 --> 22:53.038
Same as always. There's still a pecking
order, and they still fight all the time.

22:53.121 --> 22:55.624
-Ugh.
-But they stopped bothering me.

22:55.707 --> 22:56.917
-Seriously?
-[Hyeong-ju] Yeah.

22:57.000 --> 22:59.169
-That's great.
-And how's it going for you?

22:59.878 --> 23:01.171
Are you adjusting well?

23:01.254 --> 23:03.256
[pop music plays]

23:06.468 --> 23:08.720
[Seong-hwan] Hey, wait, slow down.
Hyeong-ju's in there.

23:08.804 --> 23:10.514
Hey! What's Hyeong-ju doing here?

23:11.223 --> 23:12.557
Yo, Kim Hyeong-ju!

23:12.641 --> 23:15.102
Silly bastard, why aren't you studying
for the exam tomorrow?

23:15.185 --> 23:17.104
Hold on. Whoa, isn't that Geun-dae?

23:17.687 --> 23:19.189
-No way.
-Hi there.

23:19.272 --> 23:22.025
-Hey, careful. Don't eat too fast.
-It's too damn good.

23:22.109 --> 23:24.277
[In-beom] Stuffing his face
like a fucking pig!

23:24.361 --> 23:26.696
I've been studying so much
I gained 50 pounds.

23:26.780 --> 23:29.991
-It's not studying that's making you fat.
-[Seong-hwan] Yeah, you're right. [laughs]

23:30.075 --> 23:31.576
Hey, wait, Hyeong-ju.

23:31.660 --> 23:33.745
You were able to write
that cheat sheet, right?

23:33.829 --> 23:35.080
-Say, "Ah."
-Ah.

23:35.163 --> 23:36.790
Don't you want to share with me first?

23:36.873 --> 23:38.959
I told you.
My class doesn't have the same exams.

23:39.042 --> 23:41.002
It's the same fucking exam
for the most part.

23:41.086 --> 23:43.046
-[Seong-hwan] Yeah? Eat this.
-[yelps]

23:43.130 --> 23:44.923
-[laughter]
-[In-beom] Fuck you!

23:45.006 --> 23:46.883
-[Hyeong-ju] Hey!
-Gonna kill this fucking idiot!

23:46.967 --> 23:49.136
You two should play
rock, paper, scissors for it.

23:49.219 --> 23:50.679
[Seong-hwan] Okay. Let's go.

23:50.762 --> 23:53.432
-Rock, paper, scissors, shoot! And shoot!
-Scissors, shoot! And shoot!

23:53.515 --> 23:55.142
-[laughter]
-[Seong-hwan] This fucking guy!

23:55.225 --> 23:58.019
-[In-beom] Let's go!
-[Seong-hwan] Fine. One more time.

23:58.103 --> 24:00.689
[In-beom] Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
I won again!

24:00.772 --> 24:02.190
-I get the notes!
-[Seong-hwan] Shit!

24:03.525 --> 24:04.860
[poignant music plays]

24:14.077 --> 24:15.203
[sighs]

24:17.664 --> 24:18.748
[microwave dings]

24:21.084 --> 24:22.210
[microwave door opens]

24:24.504 --> 24:26.339
REPORT ON CHUKMYEONG HIGH

24:28.383 --> 24:30.260
BY BONG GEUN-DAE, ERPB

24:34.306 --> 24:37.726
[distant screaming]

24:45.859 --> 24:47.152
[screams]

24:54.117 --> 24:57.162
[screams]

25:04.085 --> 25:05.462
[boy 1] Hey! Stop it.

25:05.962 --> 25:07.506
Stop running, you bitch!

25:07.589 --> 25:10.300
-[boy 2] Hey, don't let her get away!
-[boy 1] Slow down!

25:10.383 --> 25:11.843
Where do you think you're going?

25:13.386 --> 25:16.640
[boy 2] Hey! Seriously,
stop fucking running! Stop right there!

25:16.723 --> 25:18.808
-[boy 1] Damn it!
-[boy 2] How is she so fucking fast?

25:18.892 --> 25:20.227
[girl 1 panting]

25:21.436 --> 25:22.562
[music fades]

25:22.646 --> 25:23.939
What now, huh?

25:24.022 --> 25:25.732
[boy 1] You crazy fucking bitch.

25:25.815 --> 25:28.193
-[boy 3] Hey.
-[girl 2] Caught you, you lunatic.

25:28.276 --> 25:29.277
-Fuck.
-[boy 1] Come here!

25:29.361 --> 25:31.571
-[boy 1 grunts]
-[girl 3 laughs]

25:31.655 --> 25:34.783
[girl 3] Oh, did that hurt you?
It must sting so bad.

25:34.866 --> 25:38.286
[girl 2] I nearly puked chasing you,
you stupid fucking bitch.

25:38.370 --> 25:41.248
-[girl 1 breathes shakily]
-Han-rim.

25:42.165 --> 25:44.876
What is it gonna take
for you to come to your senses?

25:46.419 --> 25:48.129
Who do you think you are? Joan of Arc?

25:48.213 --> 25:51.341
Why the hell did you think it was
a good idea to stand up for that outcast

25:51.424 --> 25:53.176
when you're just some loser yourself?

25:53.677 --> 25:56.096
Han-rim, who the fuck
do you think you are?

25:56.930 --> 25:59.933
-Hey, It's time to learn your lesson.
-[boy 3] Good idea.

26:00.433 --> 26:01.643
All right, come here.

26:01.726 --> 26:02.561
[girl 3 laughs]

26:03.144 --> 26:05.855
[boy 3 chuckles] We're not done yet.
I missed a bit.

26:06.481 --> 26:07.941
[Hwa-jin] What are you guys doing?

26:08.024 --> 26:09.150
[Han-rim breathes shakily]

26:11.319 --> 26:13.405
-[boy 1 sighs]
-[breathes shakily]

26:17.867 --> 26:18.868
Just some damn soldier.

26:18.952 --> 26:21.830
None of your business,
so just move along, okay?

26:21.913 --> 26:25.542
Look at this guy.
"Sir, yes, sir. At your service."

26:27.294 --> 26:29.921
We're a little busy with our friend
over here, if you don't mind.

26:30.755 --> 26:31.756
Are they your friends?

26:33.341 --> 26:36.136
We're more than friends. We're… besties.

26:37.304 --> 26:40.807
Whoa! Man, I think
there's a bug flying around.

26:40.890 --> 26:44.185
-[boy 1] Oh, you scared?
-[boy 3] Fuck, no. Scared of what?

26:44.269 --> 26:45.937
[boy 1] What a prick. [laughs]

26:46.021 --> 26:48.440
-[boy 3] I wasn’t scared. Fucking idiots.
-[girl 3 laughs]

26:48.523 --> 26:49.691
Do you want help?

26:50.400 --> 26:53.236
[breathes shakily]

26:53.320 --> 26:55.030
Just ask for my help.

26:56.114 --> 26:57.157
[Han-rim breathes shakily]

26:57.240 --> 26:59.951
The first step to getting help
is asking for help.

27:01.161 --> 27:04.039
[breathes shakily]

27:04.581 --> 27:05.582
[girl 3 laughs]

27:05.665 --> 27:07.667
[girl 2] Do you know this guy?
Is he your boyfriend?

27:07.751 --> 27:09.586
-[gags]
-[laughter]

27:09.669 --> 27:12.255
[girl 3] That's disgusting. [laughs]

27:12.339 --> 27:14.424
[girl 2] How did this loser
even get a boyfriend?

27:14.507 --> 27:15.467
[girl 3 laughs]

27:16.593 --> 27:20.013
[girl 3] No way! She's crying. [laughs]

27:21.973 --> 27:24.017
[boy 2] Oh, he's so cool. Mr. Cool Guy.

27:24.100 --> 27:26.519
-Look, he's leaving.
-[boy 3] Good. He's fucking leaving.

27:27.395 --> 27:30.023
[boy 2] Oh my God,
she just grabbed his leg.

27:30.106 --> 27:31.149
[poignant music plays]

27:33.985 --> 27:35.111
[boy 1] She's so pathetic.

27:36.154 --> 27:37.072
Mister,

27:38.198 --> 27:39.491
please help me.

27:43.662 --> 27:45.830
-Okay, I got you.
-[Han-rim cries]

27:48.416 --> 27:49.709
[boy 2] She's still crying.

27:53.171 --> 27:54.130
[boy 3 sighs]

27:55.840 --> 27:57.550
What do you think you're gonna do?

27:57.634 --> 28:01.388
[scoffs] You're just a soldier.
You can't touch me. I'm just a kid.

28:02.138 --> 28:03.390
Do you think I care?

28:04.015 --> 28:05.975
-[boy 2] You can't do that!
-[boy 3] Ow, fuck.

28:06.059 --> 28:07.852
[groans]

28:10.063 --> 28:12.315
[girl 3] Let's get out of here.
He's fucking crazy.

28:12.399 --> 28:16.069
-[boy 2] Hey, wait for me, assholes!
-[boy 3] That hurts so fucking bad.

28:16.152 --> 28:17.862
[poignant music continues]

28:27.330 --> 28:28.415
[Hwa-jin] Give me your hand.

28:29.124 --> 28:31.459
♪ Oh, love ♪

28:31.543 --> 28:37.048
♪ Doesn't have to be hard ♪

28:39.008 --> 28:41.177
♪ Just simple as us ♪

28:41.261 --> 28:43.513
♪ Oh love ♪

28:43.596 --> 28:49.102
♪ Doesn't have to be hard… ♪

28:49.185 --> 28:51.813
[panting]

28:54.482 --> 28:55.400
[music fades]

28:58.987 --> 29:01.322
-[Hwa-jin] Thank you for the tea.
-[Mr. Cheon] Of course.

29:04.492 --> 29:05.577
Ah. Mm.

29:05.660 --> 29:09.080
[clicks tongue] All right,
let's get started, then.

29:09.914 --> 29:13.501
So I was amazed to see
that all the top students in the school

29:13.585 --> 29:15.879
are all a part of your class, Mr. Cheon.

29:15.962 --> 29:20.049
Yes, well, you see, all those students
come from upper-class, affluent families.

29:20.133 --> 29:23.928
The other teachers didn't want
that pressure, so I took it upon myself.

29:24.012 --> 29:26.473
You really are quite amazing.
Thank you for your service.

29:26.556 --> 29:28.349
-No, it's my pleasure.
-[Hwa-jin chuckles]

29:28.933 --> 29:31.519
Something that I didn't know
was this Noavis.

29:31.603 --> 29:34.898
I see all your top students attend this
private academy. Except Park Hyeon-ung.

29:34.981 --> 29:37.692
Hm. Have you heard about Noavis?

29:38.943 --> 29:42.155
[clears throat] Sure.
It's quite a reputable academy

29:42.238 --> 29:43.948
that only accepts the best.

29:44.783 --> 29:47.911
[Hwa-jin] You're right. So I can imagine
how disappointed they must be.

29:47.994 --> 29:49.746
I mean, when you think about it,

29:49.829 --> 29:53.625
the top student, Park Hyeon-ung,
didn't even attend their academy.

29:54.542 --> 29:56.586
From what I understand,
all these top academies

29:56.669 --> 30:00.089
are fighting amongst themselves
to have the best students join them.

30:00.882 --> 30:03.384
-Well, it's very competitive.
-[Hwa-jin chuckles]

30:04.260 --> 30:06.054
Then, let's imagine this, hm?

30:07.764 --> 30:11.518
If Hyeon-ung isn't allowed to take his
exams because of what happened at school,

30:12.018 --> 30:15.021
then who is the party
that benefits the most?

30:15.104 --> 30:17.774
Is it Noavis
who he has been a thorn in the side of?

30:17.857 --> 30:20.026
Is it all the students
who would move up in the ranks

30:20.109 --> 30:21.361
due to Hyeon-ung dropping out?

30:21.945 --> 30:27.659
Or could it be one student in particular
who would move into the top ten?

30:27.742 --> 30:30.620
For example, Jung Su-jeong.

30:31.371 --> 30:34.499
Inspector, why don't you
get right to the point?

30:34.582 --> 30:36.584
[tense music plays]

30:40.088 --> 30:43.716
Mr. Cheon, do you happen to know
a student named Han Ye-ri?

30:44.634 --> 30:46.010
I'm not sure.

30:46.094 --> 30:50.014
Well, before this case, we were asked
to investigate Soyeon Girls' High School.

30:50.098 --> 30:51.891
She was a student there.
You don't know her?

30:54.644 --> 30:57.355
[chuckles] Sir, you were actually
her middle school teacher.

31:00.942 --> 31:02.318
Yes, I remember her now.

31:02.819 --> 31:06.698
Good. So I spoke with Ye-ri.
She told me that her grades were great.

31:06.781 --> 31:09.367
She was preparing to enroll
here at Chukmyeong High,

31:09.868 --> 31:13.288
but in the end, wasn't able to come here
because she failed her exam.

31:13.371 --> 31:14.414
How curious.

31:14.497 --> 31:15.707
[Hwa-jin] Isn't it?

31:15.790 --> 31:18.501
And since she wasn't able
to attend Chukmyeong High,

31:18.585 --> 31:22.755
the last person to get in
was the one and only Jung Su-jeong.

31:23.256 --> 31:24.090
How bizarre.

31:27.635 --> 31:29.804
Now, why do you think
Ye-ri failed her exam

31:30.305 --> 31:32.807
when she was doing so well? Hm?

31:32.891 --> 31:35.852
Maybe it was because she didn't have
rich parents like Su-jeong?

31:39.689 --> 31:44.235
Is that why you fabricated that ridiculous
special class to stop her from studying?

31:44.319 --> 31:46.029
That you forced her tutor to quit?

31:46.112 --> 31:48.615
And that you would go as far
as to shut down her parents' store,

31:48.698 --> 31:50.033
just like you did to Hyeon-ung?

31:50.825 --> 31:53.494
You harassed her psychologically
to make her drop out?

32:00.627 --> 32:01.753
[Ye-ri sighs]

32:03.129 --> 32:06.966
What do you want? Haven't you
done enough to make my life miserable?

32:07.050 --> 32:09.344
What more do you want from me now, mister?

32:09.844 --> 32:10.762
Huh?

32:11.346 --> 32:12.305
[Ye-ri sighs]

32:12.388 --> 32:13.598
[music fades]

32:14.349 --> 32:16.184
I want you to tell me about a teacher.

32:17.185 --> 32:18.561
Cheon Sang-yeol.

32:19.103 --> 32:21.105
[tense music resumes]

32:25.944 --> 32:28.363
What did Cheon Sang-yeol do to you, Ye-ri?

32:30.281 --> 32:31.449
That's all I want from you.

32:42.877 --> 32:46.172
You think being one of the top students
means you're part of the elite now?

32:46.255 --> 32:50.510
Wake up, Ye-ri. Everyone is born
to be a certain social class.

32:50.593 --> 32:53.388
In your case… [scoffs]
…you're nothing but trash.

32:53.471 --> 32:57.767
[laughs] Just like your mom, and your dad,
and everyone else in your family.

32:57.850 --> 32:59.769
And that will never change.

33:00.436 --> 33:04.065
[chuckles scornfully]

33:04.148 --> 33:05.149
[sighs]

33:06.109 --> 33:08.277
Son of a bitch. [cries]

33:11.155 --> 33:13.491
[sniffles]

33:19.831 --> 33:22.208
I heard that she caused problems
at Soyeon High.

33:22.291 --> 33:24.502
She's not exactly
what I'd call trustworthy.

33:28.006 --> 33:30.174
[sighs] Mr. Cheon, I never said anything

33:30.258 --> 33:32.927
about Ye'ri's involvement
in any issues at her school.

33:33.511 --> 33:36.264
Just a second ago,
you didn't seem to remember her at all.

33:36.889 --> 33:40.810
But it's clear to me now that you're
well-informed about events at Soyeon High.

33:40.893 --> 33:43.896
I just assumed that the Bureau was there
to resolve an issue.

33:44.731 --> 33:45.690
So…

33:47.942 --> 33:49.944
whatever game you're playing,

33:50.445 --> 33:51.779
it's time to stop.

33:52.822 --> 33:54.282
Let's talk about Hyeon-ung.

33:55.658 --> 33:59.287
You know, that student
you seem to be so preoccupied with.

34:02.040 --> 34:04.000
I'll make sure that he takes his exam.

34:06.961 --> 34:08.463
Hyeon-ung will take the exam?

34:12.467 --> 34:13.718
Thank you, Inspector.

34:13.801 --> 34:14.635
[music stops]

34:17.847 --> 34:21.267
I, for one,
do believe in the potential of the Bureau.

34:22.226 --> 34:23.061
[chuckles]

34:31.569 --> 34:33.154
[sighs]

34:39.452 --> 34:41.913
-[girl] Isn't that too much?
-You're right, maybe it is.

34:42.914 --> 34:44.082
-Hey, is that Hyeon-ung?
-What?

34:44.832 --> 34:47.126
-[boy] What's he doing here?
-What the hell?

34:50.546 --> 34:52.590
The balls to come back here
after what he did.

34:52.673 --> 34:54.509
[girl] Some people have no shame.

34:54.592 --> 34:56.677
[boy] Seriously, I can't believe
he wasn't expelled.

34:56.761 --> 34:59.180
If I did that, I'd be too ashamed
to show my face.

35:06.854 --> 35:08.856
[birds chirp]

35:20.701 --> 35:22.620
[woman] What the hell are you playing at?

35:22.703 --> 35:25.790
Why am I hearing
that Hyeon-ung will be taking the exam?

35:25.873 --> 35:29.210
I told you that if Su-jeong
is to make up for her poor performances

35:29.293 --> 35:30.461
and breach the top ten,

35:30.545 --> 35:34.132
Hyeon-ung must not be allowed
to write this next exam. Is that clear?

35:35.049 --> 35:36.134
Please, have a drink.

35:36.217 --> 35:39.470
I'm afraid you must do this for me,
or you'll never make superintendent.

35:40.680 --> 35:44.684
How come all your other students manage
to make the top ten, but not my daughter?

35:44.767 --> 35:47.520
I'm paying you tenfold
what the others are. Is that not enough?

35:47.603 --> 35:48.896
Just shut it, will you?

35:49.605 --> 35:51.732
I can't change
that your daughter's a fool, you know?

35:51.816 --> 35:53.151
What did you say?

35:53.234 --> 35:55.486
You said it yourself.
Everyone does well except Su-jeong.

35:56.070 --> 35:58.406
She keeps spinning her wheels,
but she's going nowhere.

35:58.489 --> 36:00.324
How dare you speak this way
about my daughter?

36:00.408 --> 36:03.995
And the superintendent job, I can easily
get that without your support.

36:04.078 --> 36:06.622
I'm not the one who has
the most to lose here. You are.

36:06.706 --> 36:08.374
Su-jeong needs me to get to college.

36:10.418 --> 36:13.254
So please,
just stay out of this, all right?

36:13.838 --> 36:15.548
Let me take care of this.

36:15.631 --> 36:18.134
And we're in a nice establishment.
Show some class.

36:20.887 --> 36:21.971
[sighs]

36:23.014 --> 36:25.016
[beeping]

36:31.564 --> 36:32.773
Oh! You scared me.

36:36.027 --> 36:37.320
What are these?

36:37.403 --> 36:38.821
-Hold them for me.
-What?

36:39.447 --> 36:41.073
[Geun-dae gasps]

36:42.450 --> 36:44.994
Aren't you over it yet?
You've been running around for hours.

36:45.077 --> 36:46.537
-No, I'm not over it.
-Oh!

36:46.621 --> 36:48.331
-[Geun-dae gasps]
-[grunts]

36:48.414 --> 36:49.290
[panting]

36:49.957 --> 36:52.919
Han-rim, it's already late, and I need
to get more RAM for my computer.

36:53.002 --> 36:55.963
[Han-rim grunts] Damn it! [sighs]

36:56.047 --> 36:57.757
Why are you so angry anyways?

36:57.840 --> 36:59.133
[Han-rim] God damn it.

36:59.217 --> 37:01.093
It's because of the inspector.

37:01.677 --> 37:05.223
-He's just not the man I thought I knew.
-What?

37:05.306 --> 37:08.476
He isn't even interested
in what Hyeon-ung has to say, you know?

37:08.559 --> 37:11.437
All that interests him
is his hero, Mr. Cheon!

37:11.520 --> 37:14.899
-It's a personal vendetta, that's all.
-[Geun-dae] That's not it. You're wrong!

37:15.650 --> 37:16.651
[music fades]

37:16.734 --> 37:17.735
Then what's it about?

37:17.818 --> 37:20.863
Ever since the inspector came back
from his visit with Han Ye-ri

37:20.947 --> 37:23.157
he's spent all his time
investigating Mr. Cheon.

37:23.950 --> 37:27.870
And that's why he told me to look into
the top students in Mr. Cheon's class.

37:27.954 --> 37:31.916
That's why I looked into the Noavis
Institute, and went to pay them a visit.

37:32.833 --> 37:34.502
-Really?
-Yeah.

37:35.086 --> 37:37.463
-[Geun-dae sighs]
-Then tell me why nobody told me about it?

37:38.422 --> 37:39.340
Huh?

37:39.423 --> 37:44.720
Because, well, apparently,
you aren't very good at deceiving people,

37:44.804 --> 37:47.556
and are kind of a bad liar,
or so I'm told.

37:49.767 --> 37:52.687
-[sighs]
-[Geun-dae] What are you doing?

37:53.271 --> 37:54.397
-[Han-rim] Shit.
-Whoa!

37:56.691 --> 38:00.111
[Han-rim screams]

38:00.611 --> 38:03.906
[screams]

38:06.158 --> 38:07.576
-Deputy Bong.
-What?

38:08.369 --> 38:10.830
-Why's she running?
-[Han-rim screams]

38:10.913 --> 38:14.750
She says that she's running
because she's ashamed of herself.

38:15.459 --> 38:17.211
Ah.

38:18.087 --> 38:20.506
You gotta learn to slow down!

38:22.049 --> 38:24.844
-[panting]
-[gentle music plays]

38:30.182 --> 38:32.351
[panting]

38:37.940 --> 38:39.358
You lied to me.

38:40.776 --> 38:44.322
Why did you pretend all this time
that you were a fan of Mr. Cheon?

38:44.947 --> 38:47.408
That's where you're wrong.
It wasn't a lie at all.

38:48.117 --> 38:49.744
I actually was a fan of his.

38:52.663 --> 38:55.374
I was just hoping that he really was
an inspirational figure.

38:58.169 --> 38:59.170
[exhales]

39:00.254 --> 39:04.508
How come you didn't trust me enough?
You didn't say a single word to me.

39:05.509 --> 39:08.721
I wish you would've told me something.
To hide your plan from me, of all people.

39:08.804 --> 39:09.805
I just can't…

39:09.889 --> 39:12.475
I thought that
I couldn't trust you anymore.

39:12.975 --> 39:15.978
You made me think
that I didn't know you this whole time!

39:18.147 --> 39:20.024
[breathes shakily]

39:21.734 --> 39:22.568
Han-rim.

39:24.153 --> 39:25.112
Yeah?!

39:25.196 --> 39:26.614
You've known me how long?

39:30.826 --> 39:31.994
Just follow my lead.

39:36.665 --> 39:37.666
Are we clear?

39:39.752 --> 39:41.837
Yes, sir! We're clear! [cries]

39:41.921 --> 39:43.964
[Hwa-jin] This is
all because of that bastard Cheon.

39:44.048 --> 39:46.175
Shit. [cries]

39:46.967 --> 39:49.887
He's not gonna stand by and wait.
We have to keep an eye on him.

39:51.806 --> 39:54.183
Where are you going, Deputy Bong?
We've got work to do.

39:55.267 --> 39:56.227
Well, I just--

39:56.310 --> 39:58.187
Deputy Director,
didn't I just give you an order?

39:58.270 --> 39:59.647
[man] Inspector Na Hwa-jin?

39:59.730 --> 40:00.689
[music stops]

40:03.901 --> 40:06.862
We're with the police.
We received some disturbing reports,

40:06.946 --> 40:10.408
which claim that you've used
excessive force against innocent students

40:10.491 --> 40:12.410
during your tenure
at Daehan and Guun High.

40:13.244 --> 40:14.120
[exhales]

40:15.329 --> 40:18.416
Minister, we've been authorized
to execute a search and seizure mandate,

40:18.499 --> 40:20.418
further to allegations
of abuse of authority

40:20.501 --> 40:22.920
by the Educational Rights
Protection Bureau.

40:23.003 --> 40:24.588
[reporter] The public prosecutor revealed

40:24.672 --> 40:26.757
that they are investigating
Minister Choi Gang-seok

40:26.841 --> 40:28.175
on charges of tax evasion.

40:28.259 --> 40:30.761
The Minister is already in the spotlight
after he was accused

40:30.845 --> 40:34.056
of using Educations Rights Protection
Bureau for his own personal revenge.

40:34.140 --> 40:36.350
[woman 1] They were here
to protect educational rights,

40:36.434 --> 40:39.437
so I never imagined that they would
pursue teachers this way.

40:39.520 --> 40:41.939
And especially not to go after
someone like Mr. Cheon.

40:42.022 --> 40:44.400
What do you think of
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau

40:44.483 --> 40:45.776
investigation on Cheon Sang-yeol?

40:45.860 --> 40:48.404
I think they rushed into it
without any proof.

40:48.487 --> 40:50.156
Especially with the recent revelations

40:50.239 --> 40:53.200
that the Bureau seems to have been created
for selfish reasons

40:53.284 --> 40:56.328
by the father and fiancé of the teacher
who was murdered two years ago.

40:56.412 --> 40:59.081
It seems they have now switched
from targeting students

40:59.165 --> 41:01.125
to targeting teachers
in order to muddy the waters.

41:01.208 --> 41:04.420
That's what I believe was the motivation
behind targeting Cheon Sang-yeol,

41:04.503 --> 41:06.297
whose character is beyond repro--

41:08.257 --> 41:11.093
It seems that Gang-seok
has missed the mark on this one.

41:11.177 --> 41:13.262
Should we leak some stories to the press?

41:14.805 --> 41:18.225
Sir, what if we cornered the Bureau
and forced them to impeach the president?

41:18.309 --> 41:20.478
"It would appear
that the Minister of Education

41:20.561 --> 41:23.564
has fooled everybody
with his plans for the ERPB."

41:24.482 --> 41:27.193
This might be the right moment
to put the blame on him.

41:31.155 --> 41:33.199
[Gi-tae sighs]

41:36.118 --> 41:38.537
Tell everyone that
we're calling a Board meeting.

41:38.621 --> 41:40.498
[tense music plays]

41:40.998 --> 41:43.834
Minister, do you admit that
there was a clear conflict of interest

41:43.918 --> 41:46.754
during the hiring process
of Inspector Na Hwa-jin?

41:54.428 --> 41:55.721
[Hwa-jin sighs]

41:57.806 --> 42:00.559
It all happened
exactly the way you predicted it would.

42:00.643 --> 42:02.520
You have to admit he's impressive.

42:02.603 --> 42:06.023
The media, law enforcement,
the taxman, and the prosecutor.

42:06.106 --> 42:07.816
Getting all of them to work together,

42:07.900 --> 42:10.152
I don't know if the president
could even achieve that.

42:10.236 --> 42:13.948
It's hardly the right time to talk about
that. We need to get out of this place.

42:14.031 --> 42:17.535
[sighs] It's actually better
for us to stay here until next week.

42:17.618 --> 42:18.827
Why would we stay here?

42:21.330 --> 42:23.666
Because next week
is when they have the exam.

42:24.291 --> 42:26.919
And until then,
we need to keep a very low profile.

42:27.002 --> 42:28.295
God damn it.

42:28.796 --> 42:30.756
SN is N squared AL.

42:30.839 --> 42:33.259
The moment you see this,
something should pop up in your minds.

42:33.342 --> 42:35.052
Oh. Good evening, sir.

42:37.137 --> 42:39.265
Everybody, let's make sure
we understand this.

42:39.348 --> 42:41.350
When we see this,
we should remember the formula

42:41.433 --> 42:44.853
N plus one squared times AN
plus one minus…

42:44.937 --> 42:46.981
Oh, good evening. Please, take a seat.

42:47.064 --> 42:49.066
[uneasy music plays]

42:52.319 --> 42:53.279
[Mr. Cheon exhales]

42:53.362 --> 42:55.864
I saw on the news that the Bureau
won't be a problem anymore.

42:55.948 --> 42:59.660
I was able to pull a few strings.
Your help also didn't go unnoticed.

42:59.743 --> 43:01.745
Oh, it was nothing. [chuckles]

43:02.538 --> 43:04.373
That's enough talk about the Bureau.

43:04.957 --> 43:06.458
What will you do to help my daughter?

43:09.128 --> 43:10.921
Don't worry about that.

43:15.175 --> 43:16.218
[cell phone buzzes]

43:22.391 --> 43:23.517
[gasps]

43:24.101 --> 43:25.728
[woman] Is this what I think it is?

43:25.811 --> 43:27.688
Just tell your daughter
to memorize it all.

43:27.771 --> 43:30.858
And if she can't figure this one out,
well, I can't help her.

43:30.941 --> 43:34.945
[gasps] You haven't shared it
with any other students, have you?

43:36.030 --> 43:39.366
I'm sure you'll remember this, ma'am,
when the time comes for your help.

43:39.450 --> 43:41.452
Oh, don't you worry about that. [laughs]

43:41.535 --> 43:44.163
You have my support.
I'll be there for the fundraiser.

43:44.246 --> 43:48.751
[chuckles] As long as the exam goes well,
the position of superintendent is yours.

43:48.834 --> 43:50.586
[laughs] Stop!

43:50.669 --> 43:51.629
[laughs]

43:51.712 --> 43:54.506
[both laugh]

43:54.590 --> 43:58.844
Well, basically my job is to provide
logistical support and backup to the team.

43:59.345 --> 44:02.556
If they need specific documents
or any additional information--

44:02.640 --> 44:04.808
Officer, don't waste your time
interviewing this man.

44:06.018 --> 44:09.897
He's a grade one civil servant.
He simply does whatever he's told to do.

44:11.106 --> 44:13.317
You're just wasting your time with him.

44:16.820 --> 44:18.864
-Deputy Bong!
-Oh!

44:19.865 --> 44:22.660
The officers told me
that I was free to leave now, so…

44:23.369 --> 44:24.870
Go and print your request.

44:26.955 --> 44:30.709
-Sorry? I'm not sure what you mean?
-Your transfer of assignment request.

44:30.793 --> 44:31.710
I'll sign off on it.

44:31.794 --> 44:34.880
Print it out and bring it to me.
Isn't that what you wanted?

44:34.963 --> 44:37.883
Uh, actually, sir,
I thought about it again,

44:37.966 --> 44:39.843
and I think I might have changed my mind.

44:39.927 --> 44:41.303
I told you to bring it to me!

44:41.387 --> 44:43.055
I've thought about it, and I don't think--

44:43.138 --> 44:44.473
I told you to go!

44:45.349 --> 44:46.934
[funky music plays]

44:47.017 --> 44:48.060
-[Geun-dae sighs]
-[sighs]

44:48.143 --> 44:49.770
[sighs]

44:50.646 --> 44:51.897
[sighs] Yes, sir.

44:53.273 --> 44:55.317
-You requested a transfer?
-[Geun-dae] But I changed--

44:55.401 --> 44:56.485
Didn't you hear what I said?

44:56.568 --> 44:58.445
Yes, sir. I'll go and print it right now.

45:00.614 --> 45:01.990
I AM REQUESTING A TRANSFER OF…

45:05.577 --> 45:06.495
TRANSFER APPLICATION

45:06.578 --> 45:08.080
[Geun-dae] Just take another look.

45:08.914 --> 45:09.748
I, uh…

45:11.875 --> 45:13.085
Uh…

45:15.462 --> 45:16.755
[Han-rim huffs]

45:17.423 --> 45:21.927
With the way things are now, nothing good
will come of you staying with the Bureau.

45:22.010 --> 45:23.429
Inspector Na Hwa-jin,

45:24.012 --> 45:25.264
would you sign this?

45:28.434 --> 45:31.437
I don't want you to feel guilty,
so stand tall.

45:31.520 --> 45:33.897
[chuckles] You have no reason
to be ashamed.

45:49.371 --> 45:50.748
[Han-rim] Goodbye, Geun-dae.

45:56.211 --> 45:57.171
[music stops]

46:00.716 --> 46:03.010
-[pen clatters]
-Oh, sorry about that.

46:04.261 --> 46:06.597
-[laughs]
-[boy laughs]

46:06.680 --> 46:09.767
-What are you looking at?
-[girl 1] Don't be a douche. Pick it up.

46:11.977 --> 46:14.146
[girl 2] Aw, you're going to make him cry.

46:16.231 --> 46:17.691
Just look at this guy.

46:20.611 --> 46:21.987
Good morning, everyone.

46:23.947 --> 46:26.283
Please put your textbooks and phones away.

46:40.798 --> 46:42.341
Hyeon-ung, best of luck.

46:44.968 --> 46:46.178
[tense music plays]

47:14.998 --> 47:15.958
Goodbye, sir.

47:16.542 --> 47:18.001
-[Han-rim] Goodbye, sir.
-Great job.

47:18.502 --> 47:21.296
[man] What was the real reason
you founded the ERPB?

47:21.797 --> 47:24.508
Was it for revenge?
Was it because of your murdered daughter?

47:25.676 --> 47:28.762
Or was it actually a sham
to use your dead daughter for sympathy

47:28.846 --> 47:30.013
and gain political power?

47:30.097 --> 47:32.057
Why was an innocent man
like Cheon Sang-yeol

47:32.140 --> 47:33.851
deemed a target by your Bureau?

47:33.934 --> 47:35.853
You saw that you were
losing the public's support,

47:35.936 --> 47:37.646
so you used him as a distraction.

47:42.860 --> 47:44.903
EXAM MANAGEMENT OFFICE
RESTRICTED AREA

47:44.987 --> 47:46.071
[music stops]

47:49.783 --> 47:50.868
EXAM MARKING PROGRAM

47:50.951 --> 47:53.245
What? Let me look at that one, please.

47:57.457 --> 47:59.293
JUNG SU-JEONG
SUBJECT: CALCULUS

47:59.376 --> 48:00.419
This is right.

48:03.672 --> 48:05.215
[hums]

48:05.299 --> 48:08.260
JUNG SU-JEONG, SCORE: 0

48:09.636 --> 48:11.889
Excuse me, would you pass me
the math papers?

48:13.140 --> 48:13.974
Here.

48:17.895 --> 48:19.730
-And the English one?
-[woman] Here it is.

48:23.275 --> 48:25.277
What the… Wait!

48:26.528 --> 48:28.864
[suspenseful music plays]

48:34.703 --> 48:35.746
[music stops]

48:35.829 --> 48:37.039
Stop the exam right now!

48:37.122 --> 48:40.250
-I'm sorry, I don't understand.
-[Mr. Cheon] Stop the exam immediately!

48:40.334 --> 48:42.419
Everyone, send your papers
to the front! Now!

48:42.502 --> 48:44.254
Sir, the examination period
isn't over yet.

48:44.338 --> 48:47.591
How did this… Why are you still writing?
Put your pencils down!

48:48.091 --> 48:50.010
-This isn't the right exam paper.
-[Hwa-jin] Wait!

48:53.388 --> 48:54.222
But…

48:55.432 --> 48:56.683
The exam's not over yet.

48:56.767 --> 48:57.809
No.

48:58.310 --> 49:01.063
-You all heard what I said.
-Everyone, sit down.

49:01.688 --> 49:03.899
Don't listen to him. Finish your exams.

49:05.817 --> 49:06.985
Would you look at that?

49:08.111 --> 49:09.780
You seem to be very upset about this exam.

49:09.863 --> 49:13.617
Mr. Cheon, is there any specific reason
why you would want them to stop?

49:15.661 --> 49:18.664
Somebody switched them.
There'll be an investigation.

49:18.747 --> 49:21.583
-This exam will be voided and retaken.
-No. No, it won't be voided.

49:21.667 --> 49:23.585
Somebody switched the papers! It won't…

49:27.047 --> 49:28.298
[quiet rock music plays]

49:28.382 --> 49:30.717
It was the Bureau that decided
to switch the exams.

49:31.677 --> 49:33.804
But how did you… You were all in jail.

49:33.887 --> 49:36.682
That's correct. We were all being held
at the police station.

49:36.765 --> 49:39.226
So, how did we manage to switch them?

49:39.977 --> 49:41.311
Inspector Na Hwa-jin,

49:42.145 --> 49:43.271
would you sign this?

49:49.027 --> 49:51.488
SWITCH THE EXAM PAPERS

49:55.617 --> 49:57.285
TEAM LEADER
NA_HWAJIN@SUFFY.COM

49:57.369 --> 49:59.246
CHEON SANG-YEOL SON OF A BITCH

50:04.376 --> 50:05.544
CHUKMYEONG HIGH GUIDE.PDF

50:05.627 --> 50:08.171
PS I'M STEALING THEM.
MY HIGH SCHOOL DREAMS HAVE COME TRUE

50:37.701 --> 50:41.121
You've admitted to tampering with
the exams. You don't have that authority!

50:41.204 --> 50:43.248
Give me your papers.
Stop writing. Stop it, I said!

50:43.331 --> 50:45.208
You listen to me, you little-- [screams]

50:45.292 --> 50:46.543
Let go! [screams]

50:47.169 --> 50:49.254
Stop it! [groans]

50:49.337 --> 50:50.922
Let go, you bastard! [screams]

50:51.506 --> 50:55.010
-[groans]
-[teacher] What's going on here?

50:55.093 --> 50:56.303
[groans]

50:56.386 --> 50:59.306
Disrupting students during an exam
is strictly forbidden.

50:59.389 --> 51:00.807
Those rules still apply to you.

51:02.267 --> 51:03.101
You bastard.

51:07.022 --> 51:09.066
Who do you think you are?

51:09.149 --> 51:11.068
-[grunting]
-[boy] Mr. Cheon!

51:11.151 --> 51:13.236
[groans] Damn you,
you piece of shit. Just…

51:13.320 --> 51:14.613
[gasps]

51:14.696 --> 51:16.114
[Mr. Cheon breathes shakily]

51:17.824 --> 51:19.576
[classical music plays on TV]

51:26.500 --> 51:28.502
ERPB SPECIAL PROJECT

51:28.585 --> 51:31.630
Hello, hello. Mic test.
Testing, testing, one two, one two.

51:32.130 --> 51:35.008
Hello everybody. May I have your attention
for one moment?

51:35.092 --> 51:37.469
We ask for just a minute
of your attention.

51:37.552 --> 51:41.598
If you could please put your pencils down
and bring your attention to the screen,

51:41.681 --> 51:44.643
a special video
will begin shortly, entitled

51:45.393 --> 51:50.023
The Real Reason Why the Bureau
Purposely Switched the Exams.

51:50.107 --> 51:51.775
Switched.

51:51.858 --> 51:54.528
[fanfare plays]

51:55.112 --> 51:58.365
THE REASON THE ERPB
REPLACED THE EXAM PAPERS

51:58.448 --> 52:01.326
On the original exam paper
created by Mr. Cheon Sang-yeol,

52:01.409 --> 52:04.121
the answer to question one
was "one over two,"

52:04.204 --> 52:06.498
or answer number one
on the multiple-choice sheet.

52:06.581 --> 52:08.125
And what did Su-jeong put?

52:08.208 --> 52:09.334
[fanfare plays]

52:09.417 --> 52:12.170
Jung Su-jeong's answer to question one
was also…

52:12.254 --> 52:14.172
[jaunty music plays]

52:15.674 --> 52:17.425
…the same as Mr. Cheon's.

52:17.509 --> 52:19.386
[Hwa-jin] The answer
to the short-answer question

52:19.469 --> 52:20.637
in the original exam paper

52:20.720 --> 52:23.932
was, "cosine three theta is equal
to four cosine cubed theta

52:24.015 --> 52:25.433
minus three cosine theta."

52:25.517 --> 52:27.227
And Jung Su-jeong's answer was?

52:28.728 --> 52:31.898
Jung Su-jeong's answer
to this question was…

52:36.236 --> 52:39.531
"Cosine three theta
is equal to four cosine cubed theta

52:39.614 --> 52:41.575
minus three cosine theta."

52:41.658 --> 52:42.742
Like Mr. Cheon.

52:42.826 --> 52:45.996
Jung Su-jeong unknowingly
exposed Mr. Cheon's ploy.

52:46.079 --> 52:48.665
With the Bureau's altered exam,
she scored a whopping zero!

52:48.748 --> 52:51.168
A big zero in math.

52:52.127 --> 52:54.379
However, upon closer inspection…

52:54.462 --> 52:58.049
When we compared the initial exam
with Su-jeong's answer card,

52:58.133 --> 53:01.219
that's when we noticed
that she answered everything correctly.

53:01.303 --> 53:05.182
By using Mr. Cheon's exam,
she scored a perfect 100%.

53:06.016 --> 53:09.144
What's funny is that the exam questions
were actually the same.

53:09.227 --> 53:12.689
We simply altered the order
of the questions, but not the content.

53:13.190 --> 53:15.317
How could a good student,
such as Su-jeong,

53:15.400 --> 53:18.153
get zero on such a crucial exam
like this one?

53:18.236 --> 53:20.655
It's possible that she simply
didn't feel well today,

53:20.739 --> 53:23.491
or perhaps she had copied her answers,
but was one space off.

53:23.575 --> 53:26.536
But it does seem odd
that Jung Su-jeong's answer sheet

53:26.620 --> 53:29.581
would've netted her a perfect 100
on the original exam

53:29.664 --> 53:31.458
written by Cheon Sang-yeol.

53:31.541 --> 53:35.170
Statistically, this is hardly
a coincidence, no? Hm.

53:35.253 --> 53:36.254
What do you think?

53:41.384 --> 53:44.596
[Su-jeong whimpers]

53:48.808 --> 53:49.768
[gasps]

53:49.851 --> 53:52.812
Destroying evidence will put you in jail!

53:52.896 --> 53:55.732
-[Su-jeong whimpers]
-[girl] She wrote answers on her hand?

53:56.691 --> 53:58.068
[woman] Is this what I think it is?

53:58.818 --> 54:00.779
[Mr. Cheon] Tell your daughter
to memorize it all.

54:00.862 --> 54:04.282
And if she can't figure this one out,
well, I can't help her.

54:04.366 --> 54:06.660
[woman] You haven't shared it
with other students, have you?

54:07.244 --> 54:08.995
He's lying! Don't believe him!

54:09.079 --> 54:10.038
[tense music lays]

54:10.121 --> 54:11.039
I did nothing wrong.

54:12.040 --> 54:13.792
[Mr. Cheon] Tell your daughter
to memorize it.

54:13.875 --> 54:16.920
[woman gasps] You haven't shared it
with any other students?

54:17.003 --> 54:20.632
[Mr. Cheon] I'm sure you'll remember this
when the time comes for your help.

54:20.715 --> 54:22.467
[woman] Don't you worry about that!

54:22.550 --> 54:25.762
You have my support.
I'll be there for the fundraiser.

54:25.845 --> 54:31.101
[laughs] As long as the exam goes well,
the position of superintendent is yours.

54:31.726 --> 54:32.978
[woman laughs]

54:33.061 --> 54:34.020
[Mr. Cheon laughs]

54:34.104 --> 54:36.606
[both laugh]

54:37.357 --> 54:39.401
You guys don't understand.
It's all out of context.

54:39.484 --> 54:41.403
Are you kidding? What context?

54:41.486 --> 54:44.322
-[Mr. Cheon] Yeon-jun, don't you trust me?
-[boy] How could you do this?

54:44.406 --> 54:47.033
Everyone sit down, okay?
I'll explain everything.

54:47.117 --> 54:49.202
-Da-yun.
-[girl] You know how much I sacrificed!

54:49.286 --> 54:53.123
Don't forget, we've still got university,
though. Da-yun, trust me, please.

54:54.958 --> 54:55.959
[music stops]

54:56.042 --> 54:59.212
[Hwa-jin] Is that gonna give you enough
energy to study? Here, eat some more.

54:59.296 --> 55:01.339
[gentle music plays]

55:01.423 --> 55:02.882
You're quite the young man now.

55:04.134 --> 55:06.136
You just keep your head down.

55:06.845 --> 55:09.347
Leave the garbage
like Cheon Sang-yeol to me.

55:09.431 --> 55:11.016
He'll get what's coming to him.

55:13.643 --> 55:16.062
Thanks for the food. You take care.

55:17.731 --> 55:19.482
Don't stay up too late.

55:23.361 --> 55:27.907
[Mr. Cheon] It's really not what you
think. I would never do this. You know me!

55:27.991 --> 55:29.492
This whole thing is a setup!

55:29.576 --> 55:32.704
I am Hwang Gi-tae,
leader of the Mirae Daehan Party.

55:32.787 --> 55:35.582
As I had mentioned
in my last press conference,

55:35.665 --> 55:39.836
the ERPB was born from a desire
for revenge more than anything else.

55:39.919 --> 55:42.213
The bigger issue at hand here

55:42.297 --> 55:44.674
is that with
the current legislation in place,

55:44.758 --> 55:47.927
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau
has total immunity.

55:48.011 --> 55:51.473
Let me bring to your attention
Article 8 of the Bureau's policy.

55:51.556 --> 55:55.101
"All acts by an inspector carrying out
guidance duties or case investigations

55:55.185 --> 55:57.937
are exempt from the rules and laws
of behavior binding civil servants

55:58.021 --> 55:59.773
in other governmental departments."

55:59.856 --> 56:02.400
As it stands, an inspector
could commit murder if they wanted

56:02.484 --> 56:05.153
and would be exempt
from any legal consequence.

56:06.154 --> 56:08.740
You may be satisfied
with their progress right now,

56:08.823 --> 56:12.285
but I assure you, this organization
will surely bring on a terrible tragedy.

56:12.369 --> 56:14.454
-[man 1] How dare you say this?
-[man 2] Silence!

56:14.537 --> 56:16.748
-[man 3] That's enough!
-All of you, let the leader speak!

56:16.831 --> 56:18.666
-Where does he get the nerve?
-[man 4] Quiet.

56:18.750 --> 56:20.460
[Gi-tae] Minister of Education,

56:20.960 --> 56:23.129
do you remember the day of the trial
two years ago?

56:24.506 --> 56:27.717
I had the chance to speak to a prison
guard who remembers that day very well.

56:29.386 --> 56:31.805
Is guard Yoon Sun-yeol
in attendance at this moment?

56:32.680 --> 56:34.349
-Yes, sir.
-[Gi-tae] Approach the stand.

56:39.854 --> 56:43.817
Can you provide a detailed account
of what you witnessed on that day?

56:44.359 --> 56:45.985
After the trial was over,

56:46.528 --> 56:49.906
as we were escorting the prisoner,
Cho Gyu-cheol, to the prison bus,

56:49.989 --> 56:53.159
I witnessed a man driving a car
directly towards the prisoner.

56:53.243 --> 56:54.953
[engine revs]

56:57.122 --> 57:00.166
[Hwa-jin yells]

57:00.250 --> 57:03.545
Can you confirm
this is the man you saw that day?

57:04.629 --> 57:06.464
[Sun-yeol] Yes, sir, that's correct.
That's him.

57:08.508 --> 57:10.468
[Gi-tae] Although the attack
was unsuccessful,

57:10.552 --> 57:13.680
this shows that Na Hwa-jin
was ready to take him out.

57:13.763 --> 57:17.600
Knowing this, the Minister of Education
appointed him as the head inspector.

57:17.684 --> 57:20.520
Do these people have any right
to represent education?

57:20.603 --> 57:22.856
The ERPB must be abolished immediately.

57:25.191 --> 57:27.527
The witness may return to his seat.

57:28.319 --> 57:30.780
Minister Choi Gang-seok,
you have the floor.

57:30.864 --> 57:31.823
[sighs]

57:34.325 --> 57:38.621
[Gang-seok clears throat] Let me just say,
before responding to these accusations,

57:38.705 --> 57:41.708
I have far more serious matters
to present to you.

57:42.876 --> 57:45.336
As a matter of priority,
we should address these matters now.

57:45.420 --> 57:48.506
Minister, if you would please focus
on the matter at hand.

57:48.590 --> 57:51.217
-Avoiding responsibility.
-[man 5] The Minister has nothing to say!

57:51.301 --> 57:55.263
[man 4] Please, everyone, quiet down!
I will manage the proceedings.

57:55.346 --> 57:59.767
During our most recent inquiry,
we discovered proof of academic fraud

57:59.851 --> 58:02.645
taking place at Chukmyeong
Foreign Language School.

58:03.605 --> 58:07.734
We have found evidence
of an illegal, under-the-table arrangement

58:07.817 --> 58:09.944
between star teacher Cheon Sang-yeol,

58:10.028 --> 58:12.363
parents of students,
and the Noavis Institute,

58:12.447 --> 58:15.074
who conspired together
to manipulate student grades.

58:15.158 --> 58:18.453
Cheon Sang-yeol was not only
leaking exam questions ahead of time

58:18.536 --> 58:19.829
through the Noavis Institute,

58:19.913 --> 58:23.583
but also went as far as to leak
the most recent midterm exam paper

58:23.666 --> 58:25.126
in its entirety to a student.

58:25.210 --> 58:28.004
-[man 5] What? This isn't…
-[man 2] This is unheard of.

58:28.087 --> 58:33.384
If you will allow me, I will now reveal
the names of the parents who participated

58:33.468 --> 58:36.054
in the fraudulent scheme
with Cheon Sang-yeol.

58:36.137 --> 58:37.305
[intriguing music plays]

58:40.266 --> 58:43.853
Number one, wife of the chairman
of the PH Group, Kim Yeong-ran.

58:43.937 --> 58:46.856
[gasps] Oh my God! [moans]

58:46.940 --> 58:49.692
Former National Commissioner of Taxes,
Joo Hyeon-ju.

58:49.776 --> 58:53.238
The former Chief Prosecutor of Seoul
Western District Prosecutors' Office,

58:53.321 --> 58:54.322
Kim Jin-cheol.

58:54.405 --> 58:56.950
CEO of Doil Semiconductors, Lee Jin-bong.

58:57.033 --> 58:59.619
Former Minister of Environment,
Kim Hui-jin.

58:59.702 --> 59:01.955
Head Researcher at Seo Bio, Ma Seong-hun.

59:02.038 --> 59:03.665
Dermatologist Song Eun-yeong.

59:03.748 --> 59:07.085
Former Vice Minister of Culture,
Sports and Tourism, Kim Jeong-ho.

59:07.168 --> 59:09.921
CEO of Ilseong Pharmaceuticals,
Ko Tae-hyeon.

59:10.004 --> 59:12.298
CEO of Hyeonil Corporation, Kim Sang-i.

59:12.382 --> 59:14.926
Branch Manager of Bareun Bank,
Kwon Min-ho.

59:17.428 --> 59:20.431
Last but not least,
current member of the National Assembly,

59:20.932 --> 59:22.350
Lee Cheol-myeon.

59:22.433 --> 59:24.769
[reporter 1] Did he say
Lee Cheol-myeon? What?

59:25.979 --> 59:27.564
[reporter 2] It is. Look at the list!

59:27.647 --> 59:29.440
You'll pay for this. Damn you!

59:29.524 --> 59:33.194
This is slander! Slander, you hear me?
Don't believe a word out of his mouth!

59:33.278 --> 59:36.114
-I will sue you for defamation!
-Shut up!

59:36.656 --> 59:39.534
Sit down if you don't want your child's
face plastered all over the news.

59:40.451 --> 59:42.078
[camera shutters click]

59:45.039 --> 59:46.499
What's wrong with all of you?

59:46.583 --> 59:49.836
Tell me why is it that whenever the issue
of your children's education is raised,

59:49.919 --> 59:54.048
regardless of party or occupation,
you look away and keep your mouths shut?

59:55.049 --> 59:56.801
You all should be ashamed of yourselves.

59:57.552 --> 01:00:00.680
A teacher, a person who should symbolize
honesty and integrity,

01:00:00.763 --> 01:00:03.641
pressured a student
from an underprivileged background,

01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:07.562
forcing them to deliberately lower
their grades, stifling their potential.

01:00:07.645 --> 01:00:09.647
[poignant music plays]

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:12.025
How can that man call himself a teacher?

01:00:12.108 --> 01:00:15.320
Not all educators
are worthy of the title of teacher.

01:00:16.779 --> 01:00:18.406
Our Mr. President has claimed

01:00:18.489 --> 01:00:21.367
that the Bureau has only targeted
school children.

01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:24.329
Will you now claim
that we are only pursuing teachers,

01:00:24.412 --> 01:00:26.873
and that we are motivated
by personal vendetta?

01:00:29.667 --> 01:00:31.002
How dare you say this?

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:36.966
The Bureau is neither on the side
of the teachers nor the students.

01:00:38.217 --> 01:00:40.053
We are on the side of the victims.

01:00:42.680 --> 01:00:45.224
The ERPB was founded
to protect those in need,

01:00:45.808 --> 01:00:48.519
whether you are a student
being cheated of your merits,

01:00:48.603 --> 01:00:51.147
or a teacher abandoned in the line of fire
by the system.

01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:54.776
You call this a personal vendetta,
and maybe you're right.

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:56.194
Somebody needs to step up for them

01:00:56.277 --> 01:00:58.529
and take revenge
when the law does not permit it.

01:00:58.613 --> 01:01:01.908
That is the only way
that the victims will find any justice.

01:01:03.451 --> 01:01:05.912
I promise that I will find
every last person

01:01:05.995 --> 01:01:07.872
who has profited from this fraudulent scam

01:01:07.955 --> 01:01:11.292
and all the adults who were involved
in this cover-up,

01:01:11.376 --> 01:01:15.296
and I will make sure that they feel
the consequences of their actions.

01:01:17.006 --> 01:01:18.466
I will ensure that good teachers

01:01:18.549 --> 01:01:22.095
are not condemned
for the actions of the few rotten apples.

01:01:23.513 --> 01:01:24.472
I hope

01:01:25.348 --> 01:01:29.560
that the adults will act as adults,
and teachers will act as teachers.

01:01:30.269 --> 01:01:32.146
That is what the Bureau wants.

01:01:38.069 --> 01:01:39.445
This is unbelievable, isn't it?

01:01:43.783 --> 01:01:44.784
[sighs]

01:01:44.867 --> 01:01:46.994
Su-jeong, where are you?

01:01:47.078 --> 01:01:50.707
Get back here! [screams]

01:01:50.790 --> 01:01:53.668
[Gang-seok] Oh, and to those mentioned,
let me be absolutely clear,

01:01:53.751 --> 01:01:56.295
do not even think
about escaping somewhere overseas.

01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:57.255
[music stops]

01:01:57.338 --> 01:01:59.298
You've all been banned
from leaving the country.

01:02:00.717 --> 01:02:02.218
[sighs]

01:02:03.010 --> 01:02:03.970
[groans]

01:02:04.053 --> 01:02:08.015
[Hwa-jin] The equipment our dear Deputy
Bong purchased worked exceptionally well.

01:02:08.099 --> 01:02:10.226
-[Han-rim] It was expensive, apparently.
-[Geun-dae] Oh!

01:02:10.309 --> 01:02:12.645
-[Han-rim] Want me to carry it?
-No, it's fine.

01:02:13.271 --> 01:02:15.606
-Teach him how to pack his bags.
-[Hyeon-ung] Miss?

01:02:19.360 --> 01:02:21.320
["First and Last" plays]

01:02:24.198 --> 01:02:25.825
I wanted to say thank you.

01:02:36.669 --> 01:02:37.962
Thank you so much.

01:02:43.426 --> 01:02:47.889
♪ Just learning how to say goodbye… ♪

01:02:47.972 --> 01:02:49.891
Don't give up, and keep studying.

01:02:51.476 --> 01:02:56.397
♪ What did I say to you? ♪

01:03:00.193 --> 01:03:02.945
-I think you--
-Yeah, like… What? Deputy Bong?

01:03:03.446 --> 01:03:04.822
Did you want to say something?

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.532
♪ Your eyes… ♪

01:03:06.616 --> 01:03:07.742
No, it's nothing.

01:03:09.744 --> 01:03:12.330
Why are you crying? Come on, Deputy Bong.

01:03:13.122 --> 01:03:17.460
[chuckles] Off you go. Head back inside
and study. Believe in yourself.

01:03:18.377 --> 01:03:19.337
Yes, sir.

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:25.635
♪ Your eyes still… ♪

01:03:25.718 --> 01:03:28.012
All you need to do, Hyeon-ung,
is study hard.

01:03:28.513 --> 01:03:29.555
You got this.

01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:33.309
By the way, how were you able to get
that list of all the people involved?

01:03:33.392 --> 01:03:36.604
It was simple. I told them that I'd
let them off if they gave me a name.

01:03:36.687 --> 01:03:38.898
-And they gave me all of them.
-[chuckles]

01:03:38.981 --> 01:03:43.694
♪ From the day you chose me ♪

01:03:46.614 --> 01:03:51.410
♪ From the day I found you… ♪

01:03:53.621 --> 01:03:56.916
All I did was buy him a cup of tea once
while he gave me some advice.

01:03:56.999 --> 01:04:00.169
Why isn't our attorney here? We will
only speak when our attorney arrives!

01:04:00.253 --> 01:04:01.838
How dare you? Do you know who I am?

01:04:01.921 --> 01:04:05.007
Attorney Kang, why aren't you here?
I want you here right now!

01:04:05.091 --> 01:04:06.467
[officer] Sir, sit down.

01:04:07.051 --> 01:04:11.264
♪ Your eyes ♪

01:04:11.347 --> 01:04:15.142
♪ Still glowing ♪

01:04:15.935 --> 01:04:21.148
♪ Just like the day we met ♪

01:04:22.525 --> 01:04:25.528
♪ Your eyes… ♪

01:04:25.611 --> 01:04:29.198
I wanted you to see how you ruined
your student's life, Cheon Sang-yeol.

01:04:31.742 --> 01:04:32.743
[Mr. Cheon scoffs]

01:04:32.827 --> 01:04:37.290
♪ …of our first day ♪

01:04:37.373 --> 01:04:40.459
♪ How can I let you go? ♪

01:04:41.210 --> 01:04:44.171
♪ Oh, I'm not ready at all ♪

01:04:45.172 --> 01:04:49.552
♪ Let the sun rise late ♪

01:04:50.928 --> 01:04:54.724
♪ If you're not around ♪

01:04:54.807 --> 01:04:58.311
♪ Your eyes ♪

01:04:58.394 --> 01:05:02.148
♪ Still glowing ♪

01:05:02.690 --> 01:05:07.945
♪ Just like the day we met ♪

01:05:09.405 --> 01:05:13.868
♪ Your eyes ♪

01:05:13.951 --> 01:05:17.622
♪ Still holding ♪

01:05:18.122 --> 01:05:23.836
♪ The light of our first day ♪

01:05:24.337 --> 01:05:27.548
♪ How can I let you go? ♪

01:05:30.009 --> 01:05:32.094
♪ I'm gonna hunt you down ♪

01:05:32.595 --> 01:05:34.597
♪ Yeah, I ain't playing around ♪

01:05:35.348 --> 01:05:36.974
♪ I'mma take your crown ♪

01:05:37.058 --> 01:05:39.852
♪ Man, better run, gonna hunt you down ♪

01:05:40.603 --> 01:05:42.104
♪ Who's the bravest? ♪

01:05:42.688 --> 01:05:45.524
♪ Let me know
